# Distribution for CommonsLang_Rust (Darwin_x86_64)

Builds the Rust toolchain objects for the `Darwin_x86_64` slot and proves them by building a
static library that uses ring's C and assembly. It runs on a `Darwin_arm64` host.

## rustc, cargo and the host standard library

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Host.Files@1.99.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/host-Darwin_x86_64 slot=Release.Darwin_x86_64
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Darwin_x86_64", value-id: "oqkhd5rf44sgh4o5ktqwgesgs4unvavpkuhsmmiw4oicj77dfltva")\;

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Host.Files@1.99.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/host-Darwin_arm64 slot=Release.Darwin_arm64
  >   executionslot=Release.execution_abi
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Darwin_arm64", value-id: "oc4cz5ejicnhx3altlg5taeiahodfd62dolvs26ulvkjzcalw77vq")\;

## The standard library for the target

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Std.Files@1.99.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/std slot=Release.Darwin_x86_64
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Darwin_x86_64", value-id: "omex6ltd25c4ykcbcbxjao4e3krzkikdsew6gkneom3hjcnxzjcla")\;

## The CargoLock dialog (author time)

Ships the `CommonsLang_Rust.CargoLock.Bundle` dialog, which writes a crates bundle from a
`Cargo.lock`.

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.CargoLock.Export@1.0.0 -f ${RUNTIME}/CargoLock.Export.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Darwin_arm64", value-id: "ondtl7ksvkinkkkdehmvh35kyncjdfvwv6w22vxtuohytl2h5nkmq")\;

## Usage: a static library that uses ring

`assets/fixture/ring` is a Cargo workspace whose `ringlib` crate calls ring's SHA-256.
Its crates bundle came from the CargoLock dialog. cargo builds it offline.

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Cargo.F_StaticLib@1.0.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/ringlib
  >   modver=CommonsLang_Rust.Fixture.RingLib@1.0.0
  >   srcasset=CommonsLang_Rust.Apparatus.RingFixture@1.0.1 srcpath=assets/fixture/ring
  >   crates=CommonsLang_Rust.Fixture.Crates.Bundle@1.0.0 package=ringlib
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Darwin_x86_64", value-id: "oj3yczv7zawmwznwyumylcxiyzattjdeaez66jd5ugvj3zafkobiq")\;
